content.text:
Two `UserPromptSubmit` hooks are registered with no explicit `timeout` field (so they fall back to the default, which is what hit the 30s ceiling):

1. **Project-level** (`.claude/settings.json`): `entire hooks claude-code user-prompt-submit` — this is the `entire` checkpoint/session-indexing CLI (you've got `.entire/settings.json` tracked in this repo per a recent commit). Most likely culprit — it does real I/O against session/checkpoint state on every prompt, and this is a big monorepo.
2. **Global** (`~/.claude/settings.json`): `tokensave hook-prompt-submit` — also no explicit timeout.

(The other global one, `inject-test-failures.py`, already has `"timeout": 5` set, so it's not this.)

To fix: add an explicit `"timeout"` (in ms) to whichever one is slow. My money's on `entire` given its job description — try bumping it first:

```json
"UserPromptSubmit": [
  {
    "matcher": "",
    "hooks": [
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": "sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code user-prompt-submit'",
        "timeout": 15000
      }
    ]
  }
]
```

Want me to add that to `.claude/settings.json`, or would you rather test which hook is actually slow first (e.g. time `entire hooks claude-code user-prompt-submit` manually)?

